<article class="env-example" id="09FH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09FH">Example <span data-tag="09FH">9.3.2</span> <span class="named">(Prime fields)</span>.</a>  If $p$ is a prime number, then $\mathbf{Z}/(p)$ is a field, denoted $\mathbf{F}_ p$. Indeed, $(p)$ is a maximal ideal in $\mathbf{Z}$. Thus, fields may be finite: $\mathbf{F}_ p$ contains $p$ elements. </p>
